# TypeScript

Strict. `verbatimModuleSyntax`. `erasableSyntaxOnly`. Import `.ts` / `.tsx`
extensions on local files. Type-only imports use `import type`.

```ts
// ✅
import type { HealthResponse } from "@agentic-kanban/schemas";
import { healthRoutes } from "./routes/health.ts";

// ❌
import { HealthResponse } from "@agentic-kanban/schemas";
import { healthRoutes } from "./routes/health";
```

- Treat API JSON as `unknown` and parse with Zod. Never `as HealthResponse`.
- Web `tsconfig` types: `["vite/client"]` only. Do not leak `@types/bun` into `apps/web`.
- API and db: `types: ["bun"]`. Schemas: no extra `types`.
- No `baseUrl`. Web `@/*` paths live without it; Vite aliases `@` → `apps/web/src`.
- Tests import from `vite-plus/test`, not `vitest`.
